    <string name="recording_post_save_program_title">Choose a stretch</string>
    <string name="recording_stretch_instruction_calf">Step the named leg back, keep that knee straight without locking it, and its heel down. Bend the front knee gently. Use a stable wall or railing if needed.</string>
    <string name="recording_stretch_instruction_glute">Lie on your back, cross one ankle over the opposite thigh, and draw your legs gently toward your chest.</string>
    <string name="recording_stretch_instruction_hamstring">Lie back and raise one leg. Hold behind the thigh and gently draw it toward you, keeping the knee softly straight.</string>
    <string name="recording_stretch_instruction_hip_flexor">Kneel in a split stance, gently tuck your pelvis, and keep your spine neutral as you shift forward.</string>
    <string name="recording_stretch_instruction_inner_thigh">Sit tall with the soles of your feet together. Let your knees relax outward without pushing them down.</string>
    <string name="recording_stretch_instruction_quad">Hold a stable wall or railing. Bend the named knee and gently bring that heel toward your bottom, keeping knees close. Skip if support is unavailable or balance feels difficult.</string>
